Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:37:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] downloads: keep the process alive in the background on
 HarmonyOS (silent audio + wake lock)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same fix as mihon-harmony patch 0005. On HarmonyOS 卓易通 the app process
is suspended a few seconds after it leaves the foreground even though the
download queue and the library update run inside WorkManager's dataSync
foreground service: downloads stop until the app is reopened, and the idle
service keeps draining Android 15's 6-hour dataSync budget until the system
kills the app with ForegroundServiceDidNotStopInTimeException. Only audio
output keeps the container running (verified with Animeko on the same
device).

Add BackgroundKeepAlive: a ref-counted helper that, while at least one job
holds it, loops a silent PCM buffer through a MODE_STATIC AudioTrack (no
CPU, no audio focus, other apps are not ducked) and holds a partial wake
lock. DownloadJob and LibraryUpdateJob acquire it right after
setForeground(); the token is released when the worker completes, fails or
is cancelled. DownloadJob is declared as a mediaPlayback foreground service
(manifest: dataSync|mediaPlayback + permission), which has no time limit.

Everything sits behind Settings → Downloads → "Keep running in the
background (HarmonyOS)", on by default.
